#
# Counter-example for the lang: slice's thin lang:FlagshipScenarioShape: a
# gmeow:FlagshipScenario that binds ALL links — gmeow:demonstratedByExample,
# gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency, gmeow:demonstratedByProducer,
# gmeow:guardedByCounterExample, AND gmeow:enforcesFailureClass — so the shared
# cardinalities are satisfied, but gmeow:enforcesFailureClass names lang:Grammar, a real
# class that is NOT a lang:LangConformanceFailure subclass. The slice's failure-range
# sh:sparql fires, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent: an acceptance
# scenario whose enforcing failure class is not a typed conformance failure is unwired by
# value (lang:UnwiredFlagshipScenario).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecFlagshipNonFailureClass).
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:nonFailureClassScenario a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-cats-chase-mice.ttl" ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/lang/tests/cqDenotationsToFormula> ;
    gmeow:demonstratedByProducer "pipeline::stages::lang_lowering::build_corpus" ;
    gmeow:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/meaning-underspecified-denotation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass lang:Grammar .
